settings.git.lua.ph:
local diff = shikisha.git_diff(shikisha.get_var("git_tab"), {staged = true})
return shikisha.ai_ask("Describe this change in one line:

" .. diff)

ai.resolve.prompt:
The file below is a git merge conflict, exactly as git left it, including the <<<<<<< ======= >>>>>>> markers.

Work out what the file should be: keep what both sides were trying to do, and remove every marker. Do not comment, do not explain, do not fence it. Reply with the finished contents of the file and nothing else.

File: {file}

{body}

ai.commit.prompt:
Write a git commit message for the change below.

Rules: one summary line under 72 characters, in the imperative. Add a blank line and a short paragraph only if the summary cannot carry the reason. Reply with the message and nothing else -- no code fence, no preamble.
{extra}
{diff}
